---js
{
  layout: "layouts/base.njk",
  title: "Collectibles",
  seoTitle: "GTA 6 Collectibles: All Locations and 100% Checklist",
  description: "Every GTA 6 collectible set with locations grouped by region and a checklist that saves your progress toward 100%.",
  eleventyComputed: {
    sample: (data) => !!data.db.collectibles.sample,
    updated: (data) => data.db.collectibles.updated,
  },
}
---
{%- set c = db.collectibles %}
<header class="mast" style="--glow:var(--cyan)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Collectibles and 100%</p>
    <h1>Hidden Leonida</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Everything scattered across the state, counted in one place. Tick items off on each set's page and the totals here follow.</p>
    {%- if c.types.length %}
    <div class="progress total" data-progress="col:" data-total="{{ c.total }}">
      <div class="total-row"><span class="big" data-done>0</span><span class="of">of {{ c.total }} collectibles found</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><i></i></div>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</header>

{%- if not c.types.length %}
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="empty">
      <p class="kicker">Opens at launch</p>
      <h2 class="sec-h sm">Collectibles get mapped as we find them</h2>
      <p>Rockstar has not said which collectibles GTA 6 has or how many. Each set gets its own page here, with locations grouped by region and a checklist, once we have found it in the game.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- else %}
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="sec-h">The sets</h2>
    <p class="lede">Open a set for locations and its checklist.</p>
    <div class="types">
      {%- for t in c.types %}
      <div class="type" data-progress="col:{{ t.slug }}:" data-total="{{ t.total }}">
        <div class="head">
          <div><h3><a href="/collectibles/{{ t.slug }}/">{{ t.name }}</a></h3><p class="desc">{{ t.desc }}</p></div>
          <span class="count"><b data-done>0</b> / {{ t.total }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bar thin"><i></i></div>
        <p class="type-foot"><span>{{ t.items.length }} of {{ t.total }} mapped so far</span><a href="/collectibles/{{ t.slug }}/">Locations and checklist</a></p>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <button class="reset" type="button" data-reset="col:">Reset all collectibles</button>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="sec-h">Where to look</h2>
    <p class="lede">Which sets turn up in which region, for clearing the map one area at a time.</p>
    <div class="regions">
      {%- for r in regions %}
      <div class="region">
        <span class="pin">◉ {{ r.kind }}</span>
        <h3><a href="/map/{{ r.slug }}/">{{ r.short or r.name }}</a></h3>
        <div class="here">
          {%- for t in c.types %}{% if r.slug in t.regions %}<a href="/collectibles/{{ t.slug }}/">{{ t.name }}</a>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
